<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xml:lang="EN" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Neural Transplant Plast</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="publisher-id">NP</journal-id><journal-title>Journal of Neural Transplantation &#x00026; Plasticity</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0792-8483</issn><publisher><publisher-name>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">8959551</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2565301</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1155/NP.1997.49</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Morphometric Analysis of Hippocampal Pyramidal Neurons <italic>in situ</italic> and in Grafts Developing in the Anterior Eye Chambers of Young and Aged Wistar Rats</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Zhuravleva</surname><given-names>Z. N.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1"/><xref ref-type="corresp" rid="cor1">*</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Saifullina</surname><given-names>V. N.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1"/></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Zenchenko</surname><given-names>C. I.</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1"/></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="I1">Institute of Theoretical and  Experimental Biophysics, Russian Academy of Sciences, Puschino, Moscow Distr. 142292, Russia</aff><author-notes><corresp id="cor1">*Z. N. Zhuravleva</corresp></author-notes><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><year>1997</year></pub-date><volume>6</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>49</fpage><lpage>57</lpage><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 1997.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>1997</copyright-year></permissions><abstract><p>We performed a morphometric analysis of the somatic and nuclear areas in the pyramidal neurons of the hippocampal fields CA1 and CA3 <italic>in situ</italic> and in grafts developing for six weeks in the anterior eye chambers of young (3-to-9 wk.) and of aged (18-to-19.5 mos.) Wistar rats. The mean areas of the CA1 pyramidal somata and nuclei were significantly decreased in the aged animals <italic>in situ</italic>. The mean parameters of the CA3 pyramidal neurons were not changed, although their distribution was different (bimodal <italic>versus</italic> unimodal in the young animals). In both groups of recipients, the areas of CA1 neurons and of their nuclei were significantly larger in the grafted tissue than those found <italic>in situ</italic>. The areas of CA3 neurons did not show any difference in aged recipients and demonstrated only slight hypertrophy in young recipients. We concluded that the area sizes of the pyramidal cell bodies and nuclei in CA1 neurons are more sensitive than those of CA3 neurons to both aging and transplantation. The age of recipients did not significantly influence the growth and development of grafted pyramidal cells.</p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>